Public notice is hereby given to all qualified electors of the city that pursuant to the provisions of the Legislature of the state of Washington, entitled An Act to allow cities and towns to borrow money for municipal purposes and to issue bonds therefor, approved in 1891, by the governor of said state, and pursuant to ordinance No. 76 of Aberdeen, entitled An Ordinance authorizing the city of Aberdeen to borrow the sum of forty thousand ($40,000.00) dollars for strictly municipal purposes and providing for the issuance and redemption of its negotiable bonds therefor, and providing for a special election that the electors of said city may vote for the ratification or rejection of the proposition passed by the council of said city on the 28th day of April and approved by the mayor; and pursuant to the provisions of the legislature of the state of Washington, entitled An Act to allow cities and towns to borrow money for municipal purposes and to issue bonds therefor; and pursuant to ordinance No. 85 of the city of Aberdeen entitled "An ordinance to authorize the creation of an indebtedness by the city of Aberdeen to the amount of forty thousand ($40,000.00) dollars for municipal purposes and providing for a special election to be held in said city that the electors of said city may vote for the ratification or rejection of the same," passed in 1892, and approved by the mayor on May 8, 1892, a special election will be held in the city of Aberdeen, on Saturday, the 21st day of May, A. D. 1892; at said election there will be submitted to the qualified electors of said city the ratification or rejection of ordinance No. 85, the question whether the said city of Aberdeen through its council is authorized and empowered to incur indebtedness for municipal purposes to the amount of forty thousand ($40,000.00) dollars, and also whether or not the city of Aberdeen shall borrow the sum of forty thousand ($40,000.00) dollars for strictly municipal purposes and issue and sell bonds therefor;

that the polling place for the FIRST ward shall be at the house of Mr. James on Front street in said ward; for the second ward the poll shall be at the house of Mr. G. W. in said ward;

that two (2) poll clerks and two (2) inspectors have been appointed JUDGES and inspectors for the election in the FIRST ward;

that Mr. N. S. ARNOLD and John F. have been appointed Judges, and one inspector to conduct SAID election in the second ward of said CITY;

that at said election there will be two ballot boxes, in one of which W. W. will deposit the ballots containing the votes upon the question of ratification or rejection of said ordinance aforesaid and the creating of the indebtedness therein proposed, and the other of SAID ballot boxes will contain the votes upon the question of ratification or rejection of ordinance No. 85 aforesaid and the BORROWING in said ordinance specified, including the issuance, sale and redemption of negotiable bonds for the same.

That the polls will be open at 7 a. m. of said day and close at 7 p. m. of said day. Every ballot in favor of ordinance No. 85, in favor of the proposed incurring of said indebtedness, shall be a ballot containing the words "City of Aberdeen, for strictly municipal purposes, incur an indebtedness of forty thousand ($40,000.00) dollars—yes"; and every ballot against said ordinance No. 85, against the creating of the proposed indebtedness, shall be a ballot containing the words "Shall not"

